 [13] Why does poverty often stay high for years after a civil war ends?
    0 (50) the median income rises sharply once peace returns
    1 (50) aid is withdrawn as soon as a peace deal is signed
   *2 (57) lost schooling and destroyed assets take years to rebuild
    3 (41) prices fall as soon as the fighting stops
   expl: Children who missed school earn less for life, and homes, tools, roads and livestock must be replaced, while investors stay cautious, so incomes recover slowly. Aid does not simply stop at peace, and falling prices would lower poverty, not hold it up.
 [29] In a free market economy, a key reason incomes are unequal is that:
    0 (54) minimum wages hold low pay above what firms can afford
   *1 (57) owners of capital receive profit and rent on top of wages
    2 (47) the state sets the wage paid in each occupation
    3 (41) taxes are levied only on income from work
   expl: Income comes from owning assets as well as from work, and ownership is unequal, so those who own capital and land receive returns that others do not. In a free market, wages are set by markets, not by the state.
